$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for preparing
2-nitrodiphenyl ethers 3a-k, 3n-o, and 3r-t The 2-nitrodiphenyl ethers
were prepared via a modification of the published synthetic procedure.1
Ethers 3a,2 3b,3 3f,3 3h4, 3n,5 3o,6 3r-s,7 and 3t8 are known compounds.
To a mixture of potassium carbonate and the substituted phenol in DMF,
1-fluoro-2-nitrobenzene was added dropwise while stirring under nitrogen.
After 3 h at 80°C, 50 mL of water and then 30 mL of ethyl acetate were
added to the reaction mixture. The organic layer was washed with water
(50 mL x 3), and the products were obtained by removal of the EtOAc.
1-Nitro-2-(p-tolyloxy)benzene (3a): 2 p-Cresol (0.21 g, 1.9 mmol),
1-fluoro-2-nitrobenzene (205 μL, 1.9 mmol), and K2CO3 (1.3 g, 9.7 mmol)
were used. 1-(4-Methoxyphenoxy)-2-nitrobenzene (3r): 7 4-Methoxyphenol
(0.37 g, 3.0 mmol), 1-fluoro-2-nitrobenzene (317 μL, 3.0 mmol), and K2CO3
(0.83 g, 6.0 mmol) were used. The product was obtained as a yellow liquid
(0.64 g, 87%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.91 (dd, J1 = 8.1 Hz, J2 = 1.6
Hz, 1H), 7.47-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.15-7.09 (m, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H),
6.94-6.88 (m, 3H), 3.81 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Additivity of Substituent Effects in Aromatic Stacking Interactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hwang, Jungwun; Li, Ping; Carroll, William R.; Smith, Mark D.; Pellechia,
Perry J.; Shimizu, Ken D.
