$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (R)-2-[4-(4-cyano-2-fluorophenoxy) phenoxy] ethyl propanoate
(3) 3 was prepared as follows: (R)-2-(4-hydroxyphenoxy) ethyl propionate
(21.02 g, 100 mmol) was put into a 500 ml three-mouth flask, and then 100
ml DMSO was added at room temperature. To the resulting solution,
3,4-difluorobenzonitrile (15.3 g, 110 mmol), K2CO3 (16.58 g, 120 mmol)
were added and reacted for 6 h with stirring at 85°C. After cooling, the
reaction mixture was filtered. The solvent of the reaction filtrate was
washed with ice water (200 ml) and extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 200
ml). The extract was washed with an ice-cold saturated NaCl solution (3 x
200 ml) and dried over Na2SO4. After filtration, the solvent of the
mixture filtrate was finally purified by silica gel column chromatography
to give 3. Pale yellow solid, yield 86.5%. 1H NMR(CDCl3-d6)δ :
6.86-7.49(m, 7H), 4.75(m, 1H), 4.26(m, 2H), 1.64(d, 3H), 1.28(m, 3H); IR:
3453, 3076, 2986, 2576, 2221, 2065, 1731, 1621, 1397, 1063, 876, 609
cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel and highly effective chemoenzymatic synthesis of
(2R)-2-[4-(4-cyano-2-fluorophenoxy)phenoxy]butylpropanoate based on
lipase mediated transesterification
