Ethers and Esters (1a-m and 2a-d) Carvacrol (10mmol) was dissolved in an
aqueous sodium hydroxide solution (5 mL, 2N). Then adsorbent (1.5 g) was
added to this solution and stirred well. The mixture was treated in a
microwave oven for complete removal of water. To this dry powder, alkyl
halide or acid chloride (10 mmol) or α ,ω -dibromoalkane or diacid
chloride (5 mmol) was added and irradiated under microwaves at 270W at
pulses of 30s for 1-5 min. After completion of reaction (monitored by
TLC), the mixture was cooled and extracted with petroleum ether (2 x 25
mL). The extract was treated with sodium bicarbonate, washed with water,
and dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate. The removal of the solvent
afforded the products 1a-m and 2a-d (Scheme 1, Table 1). Compound 1h,
yield 87%. Bp/mp : 77°C; Lit. bp/mp : 77°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation, solid-supported reaction, solvent
removed by microwave irradiation in first stage, fly ash gives lower
yield of product while silica gives same yield of product, no solvent,
reactant assumed
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-Supported Synthesis of Bio-active Carvacrol Compounds Using
Microwaves
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Narkhede, H. P.; More, U. B.; Dalal, D. S.; Mahulikar, P. P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2008), 38(14), 2413-2418

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME117 STEP1
