$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for CuI catalyzed
Multicomponent coupling reaction: To a screw-cap test tube, was added CuI
(28.5 mg, 0.15 mmol), N,N-dimethylglycine (28 mg, 0.20 mmol),
4-bromphenyl iodide (282 mg, 1.0 mmol), amide (1.2 mmol), K3PO4 (1.06 g,
except where noted), and a magnetic stir bar. The reaction vessel was
fitted with a rubber septum. The vessel was evacuated and back-filled
with nitrogen (3 cycles). DMSO (3 mL) was added. The reaction tube was
sealed and the contents were stirred in a pre-heated oil bath at 80°C or
100°C. After the designated time period, the reaction mixture was cooled
to room temperature and phenol (1.2 mmol) was then added successively.
The mixture was stirred at 120 °C or 130°C for another designated time
and then the reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature.
The cooled mixture was directly loaded on a short silica gel column and
eluted with ethyl acetate (50 mL). The eluent was washed with brine (25
mL). The organic layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted
with ethyl acetate (3×20 mL). The combined organic phases were dried over
Na2SO4. Solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel to afford the desired product.
1-(4-(4-methoxyphenoxy)phenyl)azepan-2-one (Table 2, entry 4). Purified
by column chromatography on silica gel using ethyl acetate/petroleum
ether (1:2) as eluent to obtain the title compound as a white solid.
Yield 87%, m.p. 82-84°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ 7.11 (dt, J = 2.1 Hz,
8.9 Hz, 2H), 6.99 (dt, J = 2.3 Hz, 9.1 Hz, 2H), 6.93-6.87 (m, 4H), 3.80
(s, 3H), 3.72 (s, 2H), 2.69 (s, 2H), 1.82 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 600
MHz): δ 175.71, 156.77, 156.06, 149.93, 139.08, 127.45, 120.98, 117.87,
114.90, 55.66, 53.22, 37.63, 29.87, 28.88, 23.55. IR (cm-1) 2931, 1646,
1600, 1500, 1454, 1408, 1349, 1230, 1214, 1200, 1103, 1033, 873, 847,
827. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C19H21NO3 ([M+Na]+) 334.1414, found
334.1422.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-Catalyzed One-Pot Multicomponent Coupling Reaction of Phenols,
Amides, and 4-Bromphenyl Iodide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
