$DATUM 4-(4-penta-Fluorophenoxy)-1-allylthiobenzene (48). NaOH (0.60 g, 15 mmol)
was added to a mixture of pentafluorobenzene (1.2 mL, 10 mmol) and
compound 47 (1.7 g, 10 mmol) in DMF (10 mL) in ice-water bath. The
resulting mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 0.5 h and was
filtered. The filtrate was evaporated and the residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel to afford the desired product. Yield
2.9 g (87%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.49 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 5.05 (s,
1H), 5.08 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 5.82 - 5.90 (m, 1H), 6.91 (d, J = 8.6 Hz,
2H), 7.35 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H); 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -162.20 (dd, J
= 22.0, 17.4 Hz, 1F), -159.98 (t, J = 21.5 Hz, 1F), -154.13 (d, J = 17.4
Hz, 1F); HRMS (ESI) calcd for C15H10F5OS (M+) 333.0367, found 333.0344.
