$DATUM 4-(4-Formylphenoxy)benzonitrile (7). 4-Hydroxybenzaldehyde (6, 5.04 g,
41.3 mmol), 4-fluorobenzonitrile (5.0 g, 41.3 mmol), and K2CO3 (5.8 g, 42
mmol) were mixed in DMF (35mL) and heated to 150-160 °C using a heating
mantle. After 3 h the reaction mixture was cooled, and 2 N NaOH solution
(150 mL) was added followed by ice-water (200 mL). The product
precipitated and was collected by filtration and dried to give a brown
solid (8.0 g, 87% yield). Rf = 0.30 (3:1 hexane/EtOAc), Mp =94-95 °C; 1H
NMR (300MHz,DMSO-d6) δ 9.91 (s, 1H), 7.92 (d, J=8.4 Hz, 4 H), 7.85 (d,
J=8.5 Hz, 4H), 7.22 (d, J =3.7 Hz, 4H), 7.19 (d, J= 3.6 Hz, 4H).
