$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
1,3-Dichloro-5-(4-nitrophenoxy)-2-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)benzene
(3c). Compound 3b (0.30 g, 1.08 mmol) and NaOH (0.043 g, 1.08 mmol) were
dissolved in DMF (8 mL) and toluene (10 mL), and the mixture was heated
to remove moisture by distillation as an azeotrope with toluene. Then
1-chloro-4-nitrobenzene (0.16 g, 1.02 mmol) was added and refluxed for 7
h. When the reaction was complete, DMF was removed and saturated brine
water (5 mL) was added. The mixture was extracted by ethyl acetate. The
organic layer was dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate and filtered.
The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure to give a crude
product, which was purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel
using a mixture of petroleum ether (60-90 °C) and ethyl acetate (v/v =
20:1) as the eluent. Synthesis of
1,3-Dichloro-5-(2-chloro-4-nitrophenoxy)-2-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)benzene
(4c). Intermediate 4c was obtained as a yellow viscous liquid (yield,
87.0%) by following the same procedure as for compound 3c. 1H NMR (300 M,
CDCl3) δ 6.03 (tt, 3 J HF = 3.4 Hz, 2 J HF = 52.9 Hz, 1H, CF2CF2H), 6.86
(s, 2H, Ar-H), 6.96 (d, 4 J HH = 2.6 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.55 (dd, 4 J HH =
2.6 Hz, 3 J HH = 8.7 Hz, 1H, Ar-H),7.85 (d, 3 J HH = 8.7 Hz, 1H, Ar-H).
