$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 4-(p-nitrophenoxy)biphenyl- (II) A prebaked two-neck round
bottom flask equipped with condenser and magnetic stirrer bar was charged
with 59 mmol of 1-chloro-4-nitrobenzene (9.29 g) in excess of DMF (180
ml). Subsequently, 59mmol of biphenyl-4-ol (10 g) and anhydrous K2CO3
(8.15 g) were added to the solution and the mixture was refluxed for a
day at 120 °C under inert (N2) atmosphere. After 24 h, the reaction was
stopped and the mixture was allowed to cool down to room temperature. The
mixture was then poured into 600 ml of distilled water to yield dark
yellow precipitates of (II). The solid was collected by filtration and
repeatedly washed with distilled water. Finally, the product was
recrystallized with toluene. The crystalline structure of (II) was
confirmed by X-ray crystallographic analysis and it was reported
elsewhere [20]. 4-(p-nitrophenoxy)biphenyl- (II), yield 86%. mp. 144 °C,
molecular weight: 291.3 gmol-1. Elemental analysis (% CHN) calc. for C18
H13NO3: C, 74.22; H, 4.50; N, 4.81; and found: C, 74.37; H, 4.66; N,
4.72. FTIR (KBr, thin film, cm-1): 1593 (Ar. C=C), 1506 and 1358 (N-O),
1121 (C-O-C). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6, δ ppm): 7.39 (m, 1H), 7.49 (m,
2H), 7.63 (d, J=5.2 Hz, 2H), 7.68 (d, J=5.1 Hz, 2H), 7.29 (d, J=5.8 Hz,
2H), 7.12 (d, J=5.9 Hz, 2H), 8.26 (d, J=7.2 Hz, 2H).
