$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Tricyclic Derivatives 9, 10 (GP 5).
8-Methoxy-2-nitro-10H-dibenzo[b,f][1,4]oxazepin-11-one (9) Amide 7 (2.52
g, 7.81 mmol) was suspended in H2O (65 mL) and an aq. 2 M NaOH solution
(5 mL) was added. The mixture was refluxed for 8 h and then left to stand
at r. t. overnight. The reaction mixture was then poured into H2O (200
mL), the solid filtered off and the oxazepinone derivative 9 (1.72 g,
80%) was obtained as a brown solid. HPLC: (A) 3.8 min, 98% purity.
8-Chloro-2-nitro-10H-dibenzo[b,f][1,4]oxazepin-11-one (10) The
oxazepinone derivative 10 (2.60 g, 86%) was obtained from the benzamide 8
(3.39 g, 10.40 mmol) according to GP 5 as a solid. HPLC: (A) 4.1 min, 98%
purity. 1H NMR (200 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ (ppm) 10.93 (br s, 1H), 8.52-8.43
(m, 2H), 7.62 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H), 7.26-7.21
(m, 2H). MS (ESI), m/z: 289.0 [M-H]-.
