$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Model Reaction of 2 with 4-Phenylphenol at 90 °C. Compound 2 (0.50 g, 1.4
mmol), 4-phenylphenol (0.73 g, 4.3 mmol), DMSO (10 mL), and K2CO3 (0.69
g, 5.0 mmol) were placed in a flask equipped with an Ar inlet. The
mixture was stirred at 90 °C under Ar for 3 days as shown in Scheme 5.
After cooling, the mixture was poured into 100 mL of ethanol. The white
precipitate was washed with water and dried under vacuum overnight to
give 0.76 g (1.2 mmol) of 3 in 86% yield. The 1H NMR spectrum matched
that reported in our previous paper.16 3, yield 86%, 0.76 g, 1.2 mmol.
