$DATUM Etherifications of aryl bromides.
(4-(2,3-dimethylphenoxy)phenyl)(methyl)sulfide, Figure 7. A Flame dried
microwave vial equipped with a stir bar under a blanket of argon was
charged with Cu-Ni/C (100 mg, 8 mol % Cu), Cs2CO3 (391 mg, 1.2 equiv),
1,10-phenanthroline (90 mg, 0.5 equiv), 4-bromothioanisole (406 mg, 2
equiv), 2,3-dimethylphenol (122 mg, 1 equiv) and dioxane (3 mL). The
mixture was vigorously stirred before it was placed in the microwave
reactor and heated to 200 °C for 1800 seconds. Upon cooling, the reaction
mixture was filtered through Celite®, solvents removed and the column
chromatography with 8% EtOAc in hexanes yielded desired product in 85%
yield. (4-(2,3-dimethylphenoxy)phenyl)(methyl)sulfide, yield 85% 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.27-7.23 (2H, m), 7.08 (1H, t, 7.6Hz), 6.99 (1H, d,
J = 7.6 Hz), 6.86-6.82 (2H, m), 6.78 (1H, d, J = 8 Hz), 2.45 (3H, s),
2.33 (3H, s), 2.15 (3H, s). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 156.8, 154.3,
139.1, 130.9, 129.8, 128.9, 126.5, 125.9, 117.9, 117.7, 20.3, 17.7, 12.4.
HRMS calcd: 244.0922, found 244.0910.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper + Nickel-in-Charcoal (Cu-Ni/C): A Bimetallic, Heterogeneous
Catalyst for Cross-Couplings
