$DATUM (4-(3,5-dimethoxyphenoxy)phenyl)(methyl)sulfide, Figure 7. A Flame dried
microwave vial equipped with a stir bar under a blanket of argon was
charged with Cu- Ni/C (150 mg, 5 mol % Cu), Cs2CO3 (391 mg, 1.2 equiv),
1,10-phenanthroline (90 mg, 0.5 equiv), 4-bromothioanisole (406 mg, 2
equiv), 3,5-dimethoxyphenol (154 mg, 1 equiv) and dioxane (3 mL). The
mixture was vigorously stirred before it was placed in the microwave
reactor and heated to 200 °C for 30 min. Upon cooling, the reaction
mixture was filtered through Celite, solvents removed and the column
chromatography with 8% EtOAc in hexanes yielded product in 85% yield (238
mg). (4-(3,5-dimethoxyphenoxy)phenyl)(methyl)sulfide, yield (238 mg,
85%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.27-7.25 (2H, m), 6.98 (2H, m), 6.21
(1H, t, J = 2 Hz), 6.15 (2H, d, J = 2 Hz), 3.75 (6H, s), 2.48 (3H, s).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 161.7, 159.4, 154.8, 132.8, 129.1, 120.1,
97.1, 95.5, 55.6, 17.1. HRMS calcd for C15H16SO3 277.0905, found
277.0893.
