$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-{4-[4-(Trifluoromethyl)phenoxy]phenyl}propan-2-one. To a solution of
4-bromophenol (86.5 g, 500 mmol) in DMSO (1.25 L) was added potassium
tert-butoxide (56.1 g, 500 mmol) and 4-chlorobenzotrifluoride (90 g, 498
mmol). The mixture was stirred and heated at 160 °C for 3 days, cooled,
poured into iced water and extracted with toluene (3 x 400 mL). The
combined extracts were washed with 2 M NaOH and water, dried (MgSO4) and
the solvent evaporated to leave an oil; distillation afforded
1-bromo-4-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenoxy]benzene, yield 133.6 g, 85%. bp
94-96 °C/0.15mm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
