$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure B. Copper(I)
thiophene-2-carboxylate (CuTC)-mediatedintramolecular cyclization (with
workup under acidic conditions). 2-Chloro-8-fluoro-dibenzofuran (15c). A
10 mL microwave vial was charged with
2',5'-dichloro-5-fluoro-biphenyl-2-ol (50 mg, 0.19 mmol, 1.0 eq) and
N,N-dimethylacetamide(2.0 mL). The solution was sparged with dry nitrogen
for 2 min.Copper(I) thiophene-2-carboxylate (CuTC, 48 mg, 0.25 mmol, 1.3
equiv.) was then added. The vial was sealed under a nitrogen atmosphere
and heated under microwave irradiation at 140 °C for 20 min. The reaction
mixture was diluted with 0.2 M HCl (10 mL) and extracted with
dichloromethane (10 mL). The organic layer was washed with saturated
NaHCO3 solution (10 mL) and water (10 mL x 3), dried over Na2SO4, and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (eluent: 20-70% dichloromethane in hexanes).
2-Chloro-7-nitro-dibenzofuran, light tan solid, yield 85%. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3, δ): 8.48 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.32 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.9 Hz, 1H),
8.05 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.61 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
1H), 7.57 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, d6-DMSO, δ):
156.1, 155.0, 147.0, 129.7, 128.8, 128.4, 123.7, 122.4, 122.4,
118.9,113.9, 108.1; MS (EI+): calculated for C12H6ClNO3 [M+], 247.0; m/z
found, 246.8.
