$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Bromo-7-iodo-9H-xanthen-9-one (5b). Step 1. A RBF equipped with a
reflux condenser was charged with 4-bromophenol (15.5 g, 89.4 mmol),
2,5-diiodobenzoic acid (25.7 g, 68.7 mmol), EtOAc (0.337 ml, 3.44 mmol),
and toluene (100 mL). Cs2CO3 (44.8 g, 137 mmol) was carefully added
portionwise (gas evolution). After stirring at RT for 10 min, the mixture
was heated to 50°C for 40 min and then heated to 100°C for 20 hrs. The
reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperaure. The mixture was
filtered through Celite and the solids were washed with EtOAc. The
filtrate was diluted with water (200 mL), acidified with 2N HCl (300 mL),
and extracted with EtOAc (4 x 500 mL). The organic extract was washed
with brine and dried over sodium sulfate. The organic fractions were
concentrated under reduced pressure. Crude
2-(4-bromophenoxy)-5-iodobenzoic acid (31.1 g) as a tan oil that
solidified upon standing. Step 2. H2SO4 (73.3 ml, 1375 mmol) was added to
2-(4-bromophenoxy)-5-iodobenzoic acid (28.8 g, 68.7 mmol) at rt. The
resulting dark mixture was heated to 60°C for 45 minutes. The brown
solution was poured slowly onto ice-water (1 L) with stirring. The
resulting tan precipitant was collected by filtration, washed with water,
1 N NaOH solution, again with water, and dried under reduced pressure.
2-bromo-7-iodo-9H-xanthen-9-one (23.4 g. 85%) as a tan solid that was
used without further purification. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ ppm 8.41
(d, J=2.3 Hz, 1 H), 8.24 (d, J=2.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.17 (dd, J=8.8, 2.3 Hz, 1
H), 8.04 (dd, J=8.9, 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.68 (d, J=8.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.52 (d,
J=8.8 Hz, 1 H).
